<meta name="description" content="This Special Issue (SI) provides an expansive forum for advanced multidisciplinary research that facilitates fundamental network architecture design through analytical modeling, learning-driven protocol optimization with performance bounds, cross-layer cognition-cycle integration, practical protocol validation strategies, and broader applications in next-generation unmanned networks. We invite researchers and practitioners from communications, multi-agent systems, robotics, protocol design, edge computing, satellite communications, and control theory to help reshape this promising research frontier. This scope includes high-quality innovative research with theoretical foundations and visionary perspectives, including but not limited to the following areas:" />
